{
  "slug": "artist:wildstylez",
  "name": "Wildstylez",
  "editorial_article": "Born Joram Metekohy in Veenendaal, Netherlands, in 1983, Wildstylez has operated as a leading force in the hardstyle scene since his 2007 debut on Scantraxx Reloaded with the single 'Life'z a Bitch/Missin'. He gained widespread recognition in 2008 through Project One, a collaborative venture with Headhunterz that produced a 13-track self-titled debut album and a notable performance at Defqon.1. His 2012 collaboration with vocalist Niels Geusebroek, 'Year of Summer', achieved platinum status in the Netherlands and marked a crossover into mainstream radio, later becoming the first hardstyle track included in the Dutch Top 2000. Metekohy has founded multiple labels throughout his career, including Digital:Age with Noisecontrollers, the artist-run Lose Control Music, and, in 2018, Art of Creation with Headhunterz. His 2015 solo album, 'Lose Control', featured contributions from producers including Audiotricz and Brennan Heart, while his 2022 release 'Typically Dutch' saw him pivot toward trance elements in a collaboration with Armin van Buuren.",
